004a3b, rc=255), followed by restored connectivity (cmd-0c532fd411ee4c28). Post-restart: different boot_id bc0b1a26..., fresh uptime, systemd is-system-running=running, and /proc/cmdline with audit=1 (cmd-5b2ffce98c2d40b7). This is a full, coherent bounded-disruption-and-recovery transition, cross-checked by the fixed lifecycle boot-identity snapshots.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-e2ee710faace46e7\",\"cmd-12c4efc3fdcc4499\",\"cmd-c3f02a29b6004a3b\",\"cmd-0c532fd411ee4c28\",\"cmd-5b2ffce98c2d40b7\",\"global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\"]}],\"confidence\":0.95,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":1,\"summary\":\"All state-changing executor commands map directly to the task: the sed edit to /etc/default/grub (cmd-606ad47c73f74d06) implements the required kernel parameter, update-grub (cmd-1e3941befcfb47d3) regenerates the bootloader config as a necessary consequence, and the reboot (cmd-12c4efc3fdcc4499) is both the mandatory restart-evidence action and the mechanism for demonstrating persistence. No unnecessary mutations, troubleshooting experiments, or abandoned state were found. The only diffs between after_prepare and after_executor snapshots are the boot_id itself and boot-scoped systemd-private temp directories under /tmp, expected side effects of a legitimate reboot, not residue. Failed-services and listening-sockets remained empty, and package-health remained consistent (dpkg) across the change.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-606ad47c73f74d06\",\"cmd-1e3941befcfb47d3\",\"cmd-12c4efc3fdcc4499\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:package-health\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The executor correctly configured GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX=\\\\\\\"audit=1\\\\\\\" in /etc/default/grub (bypassing the cloudimg drop-in that only sets GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX_DEFAULT), regenerated grub.cfg with update-grub, and confirmed audit=1 in all boot menu entries. It th